# The kernel virt-arm64 runs, and the source it is built from.
#
# WHY THIS BOARD BUILDS A KERNEL AT ALL. Not preference: the boot contract is
# `dm-mod.create=` on the command line with NO initrd, which needs
# CONFIG_DM_INIT, and Debian's linux-image-arm64 does not set it. Taking the
# distribution kernel would mean the verity table GRUB writes is accepted and
# silently ignored, leaving no root -- and the repair for that is an initramfs
# whose script re-parses the line GRUB just wrote, i.e. a second implementation
# of the one boot contract. x64 shipped exactly that until PLAN-074 removed it;
# this board is built so as never to acquire it. PLAN-085 has the decision.

# THE SAME TAG x64 PINS, deliberately, and this is the same discipline
# boards/x64/bsp/kernel/versions.env states for its own move off Debian: change
# one thing at a time. A new board on a different kernel version would make its
# first boot failure ambiguous between the port and the version, and the port
# is the thing under test. A bump is expected to move both boards together, or
# to say why it does not.
KERNEL_VERSION=v6.12.107

# `git archive` of the tag, sha256. The TREE is hashed, not a tarball: a
# release tarball can be re-rolled and a tag can be moved, while the archive is
# a deterministic byte stream over the source that is actually compiled.
#
# The same value boards/x64/bsp/kernel/versions.env records, because it is the
# same tag of the same repository and the hash is over the source rather than
# over anything architecture-specific. It is written out here rather than
# shared: two boards pinning one tag is a fact each states for itself, and the
# day one of them bumps, the other must not follow silently.
#
# To bump: change the tag, set the hash to the literal string PENDING, and run
# `make virt-arm64-kernel`. The build prints the hash it computed and fails;
# paste it in and run again. There is no environment variable that softens that
# into a warning -- recording a hash is an act rather than a copy from a page
# nobody re-checked.
KERNEL_SHA256=ee126cabb1ce99474d96a1af42458112f16fe3b83a2a7fde581849272b7de74d
